# Review: AgentPlugin

The operations, the knowledge graph, identities and multi-space presence are solid and well tested:
every op exists with the specified key, `interview.test.ts`, `relay.test.ts`, `ensure-channel-chat.test.ts`,
`invite-agent.test.ts`, `admit-agent.test.ts`, `AgentSpace.test.ts` and `agent-admin-sync.test.ts` run all the
derived scenarios, the scripted interview story covers the profile panel, and EDGE mints agent spaces, issues
`IdentityAdmin` credentials and serves only registered spaces. The UI around channels has moved away from the
spec: the Activity companion no longer has a channel picker or per-channel ObjectProperties surfaces, and lists
conversations oldest first. The biggest divergence is `createAgent`, which binds the Modes, Relay, Goals and
Brain skills and leaves the Interview skill to the `Interviewer` mode.

Of 85 items: 67 done, 6 untested, 4 partial, 7 diverged, 1 missing. Findings:

- **createAgent / F-1.2:** new agents do not get the Interview skill in their Instructions; only the
  `Interviewer` mode binds it.
- **Activity companion (F-3.1, F-3.3, F-3.7):** no picker or auto-saving AgentChannels form, a status row in place
  of the backend's surface, and conversations sorted oldest first.
- **F-6.2 on EDGE:** `BrainObject._runDue` runs `RunDue` only in the agent's home space, so a watch set in another
  space is not delivered from the alarm.

