```mdl
verdict createAgent: createAgent makes an initialized agent with the Conversation skill on its first chat, but binds Modes, Relay, Goals and Brain skills, not Interview.
  status: diverged
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-agent/src/types/AgentOperation.ts#CreateAgent, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-agent/src/operations/create-agent.ts#makeAgent]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-agent/src/operations/ensure-channel-chat.test.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-agent/src/containers/AgentsSettings/create-agent.test.ts]
  walkthrough:
    - The operation declares name and instructions in and the agent ref out. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-agent/src/types/AgentOperation.ts#CreateAgent
    - makeAgent initializes the agent with base skills and the Conversation skill, and seeds the built-in modes. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-agent/src/operations/create-agent.ts#makeAgent
    - Settings' Add agent calls it, then ensureIdentity with mint while the setting is on. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-agent/src/containers/AgentsSettings/create-agent.ts#createAgent
  note: |
    `makeAgent` passes `skills: [ModesSkill, RelaySkill, GoalsSkill, BrainSkill]` to `Agent.makeInitialized` and sets
    the chat's mode to `Conversation`. The Interview skill is bound only by the built-in `Interviewer` mode
    (`operations/modes.ts#BUILTIN_MODES`), not put in every new agent's Instructions as the note says.
```

