```mdl
verdict F-6.2: In-app delivery is per origin space; EDGE's alarm runs RunDue only at the agent's home.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-agent/src/types/AgentPresence.ts#delivers, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-agent/src/operations/run-due.ts, github:dxos/edge/packages/services/compute-service/src/brain/brain-object.ts#BrainObject]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-agent/src/operations/triggers.test.ts]
  note: |
    `AgentPresence.delivers` and the trigger tests cover origin-scoped delivery and the no-origin fallback. On EDGE,
    `BrainObject._runDue` invokes `RunDue` once, in `identity.homeSpaceId` (or the legacy location), not in each space the brain
    serves, so a watch set in another space is not delivered from the alarm.
```

